{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1473767-discipline-rework-and-thoughts","id":1473767,"title":"Discipline rework and thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-01T12:20:43-08:00","id":1473767,"title":"Discipline rework and thoughts","content":"Okay, so i realized i liked the way the disciplines in requiem when they used or made allusion to the natural powers of vampires, mostly the Lashing Out mechanic.<br /> And also, i realized that the most physical innate power, the Physical Intensity, didn't interact at all with the physical disciplines, wich is kinda weird.<br /> <br /> So i tried a homebrew change : <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Physical Intensity :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of spending a point of Vitae to gain two dices in Strength, Dexterity or Stamina for the scene :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The vampire can spend one point of Vitae to activate one aspect of the Physical intensity for the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Powerful Monster :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain one dot in Strength.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the beginning of every turn, you can :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-lift an object with a size up to your success on a Strength+Athletics roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> &gt;Damages : Size (bashing). If Size&gt;=6, damages are lethal for mortals. If size&gt;=11, damages are lethal even for vampires.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-jump for your success on a Strength+Athletics roll in yards/meters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-reroll one dice on any mundane Strength related test.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Swift Monster :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain one dice to every roll using Dexterity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the beginning of every turn, you can :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-add one to your Defense and Dodge rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-increase your speed rating by one and gain one dice to every movement-related roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-increase your initiative rating by two. (Initiative Rating is Dexterity+Composure, Initiative is Initiative Rating + one dice)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Unstoppable Monster :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain one dice to every roll using Stamina.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can downgrade one point of damage every round : one aggravated becomes lethal,one lethal becomes bashing, one bashing becomes nothing. You can\u2019t downgrade damages from the sun.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Physical Disciplines :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feat : every physical discipline allows the production of Feat in a domain.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To accomplish a Feat, you expand up to your rating in the discipline Vitae.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The quantity of Vitae spent indicates the intensity of the Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1 Vitae : a very skilled and/or lucky mortal could do it.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-3 Vitae : a truly unnatural and monstrous feat.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-5 Vitae : the stuff of legends.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A test of [Rating]+Blood Potency can be used in case you need to roll some dices, for example if you\u2019re unsure the idea of the player can work, or how good it works.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feats are meant to be plot devices, and allow your players to express their creativity and the unique touch of their vampire.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Physical Disciplines :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Celerity :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quicken the Blood : you can activate the Swift Monster effect of the Physical intensity for free [Celerity] in six times.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternate System : the first [Celerity] uses of the night are free.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alacrity : the Swift Monster is modified as following :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain [Celerity+1] dice to every roll using Dexterity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the beginning of every turn, you can divide [Celerity+1] Celerity Points (CP) between those options (you can take an option more than once) :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1 CP : add one to your defense and Dodge roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1 CP : Speed rating +1, and +1 to every Movement-related roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-1 CP : Initiative rating +2.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&gt;For this system, you can use little beds with an abbreviation of the bonuses written on it.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feat of Celerity : you can spend up to Celerity Vitae point to attempt a Feat of Celerity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If those feats oppose another supernatural power, then a Clash of Will happens.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-ignore surprise.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-instantly run your speed rating, seemingly teleporting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-dodge every attack during a round, but you have to stay defensive. You can move at the same time.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-literally catch someone\u2019s voice.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a feat seems risky or too powerful, you can judge it\u2019s efficiency with a roll of Blood Potency + Celerity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Resilience :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unyielding : you can activate the Unstoppable Monster effect of the Physical intensity for free [Resilience] in six times.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternate system : the first [Resilience] uses of the night are free.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unbreakable : the Unstoppable Monster is modified as following :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain [Resilience+1] dice to every roll using Stamina.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can downgrade [Resilience+1] points of damage every round : aggravated becomes lethal, lethal becomes bashing, bashing becomes nothing. You can\u2019t downgrade damages from the sun.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feat of Resilience : you can spend up to Resilience Vitae point to attempt a Feat of Resilience.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If those feats oppose another supernatural power, then a Clash of Will happens.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-ignore one source of natural damage for a couple of rounds.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-instantly recover from one mundane penalty, be it environmental or caused by a wound.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-instantly recover from one penalty, be it environmental or caused by a wound.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-redirect something hurting you (it still hurts you, but it can hurt someone else, too) : example : grab a power line and redirect the lightning. Light up a hunter burning you with gasoline, taking the both of you ablaze.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a feat seems risky or too powerful, you can judge it\u2019s efficiency with a roll of Blood Potency + Resilience.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vigor :</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mighty : you can activate the Powerful Monster effect of the Physical intensity for free [Vigor] in six times.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternate system : the first [Vigor] uses of the night are free.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crushing Force : the Powerful Monster is modified as following :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everytime it gives a bonus or reroll of one, it becomes a bonus or reroll of [Vigor+1].</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You also gain a buff for jumping.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Modified power :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gain [Vigor+1] dot in Strength.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the beginning of every turn, you can :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-lift an object with a size up to your success on a Strength+Athletics roll * [Vigor+1].</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> &gt;Damages : Size (bashing). If Size&gt;=6, damages are lethal for mortals. If size&gt;=11, damages are lethal even for vampires.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-jump for your success on a Strength+Athletics roll in yards/meters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-reroll [Vigor+1] dice on any mundane Strength related test.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feat of Vigor : you can spend up to Vigor Vitae point to attempt a Feat of Vigor.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If those feats oppose another supernatural power, then a Clash of Will happens.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-climb and dig in pretty much anything softer than metal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-shock wave.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-create a cloud of dust by kicking the ground.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5 Vitae Feat :</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Storyteller\u2019s discretion. I bet on a local tremor.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a feat seems risky or too powerful, you can judge it\u2019s efficiency with a roll of Blood Potency + Vigor.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> In practice, it's like the physical intensity is replaced with Celerity, Vigor and Resilience o, and those disciplines amplifies it's effect further.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26829-vumerion","name":"Vumerion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}